    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research consistently shows that introducing gender diversity concepts to children in early elementary school is developmentally appropriate and beneficial for their understanding of the world. Waiting until later can lead to confusion among children who have already heard conflicting information from peers and teachers. Acknowledging different identities early fosters empathy and helps children feel safe and respected within their school environment. Ultimately, open, simple conversations are far more helpful than withholding complex topics.",
      "source": "target",
